<title>FRANCE: GAN shares suspended limit-up in Paris.</title>
<headline>GAN shares suspended limit-up in Paris.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French state-controlled insurer Groupe des Assurances Nationales (GAN) were suspended limit up at the opening of the Paris bourse on Friday, the SBF stock markets association said.</p>
<p>The share was suspended on Thursday, when the state announced a 20-billion-franc rescue plan for the insurer which it owns to the tune of 80 percent.</p>
<p>The stock was due to retrade on Friday and the SBF said a fresh attempt to requote would be made at 0915 GMT after the initial &quot;limit up&quot; suspension which is used when a stock rises by more than 10 percent.</p>
</text>
